## Delegation ladder (mandatory — follow in order, no skipping)

Before any file edit, analysis, or generation task, pick the **lowest tier that can handle it**:

| Tier | When to use | How |
|---|---|---|
| **1. Local LLM** | Free. Simple analysis, short edits, small context | `mullet_opencode` (auto-selects) or `mullet_run --providers local` |
| **2. OpenRouter** | Pay-per-token. Default cloud — cheap and reliable | `mullet_opencode` (default) or `mullet_run --providers openrouter` |
| **3. Anthropic Haiku** | Prepaid (Max plan). Substitute OpenRouter when pressure <60% | Direct in-context or `mullet_run --providers haiku` |
| **4. Anthropic Sonnet** | Prepaid (Max plan). Complex tasks; substitute when pressure <60% | Direct in-context or `mullet_run --providers sonnet` |
| **5. Kimi K2** | Pay-per-token. Large context; OpenRouter fallback | `mullet_opencode` or `mullet_run --providers kimi` |
| **6. Gemini** | Last resort — pay-per-token, expensive for large contexts | `mullet_run --providers gemini` |
| **7. Opus** | Orchestration and commit decisions only | Direct in-context |

**Hard rules:**
- File edits >5 lines → `mullet_opencode` always — never in-context Opus writing code
- Check `check_budget()` — if Anthropic pressure <60%, use Haiku/Sonnet (already paid for)
- Fall back to OpenRouter/Kimi only when pressure >60%
- Mullet's routing matrix (`routing_matrix.py`) enforces this automatically for API delegation calls

